# Git ignores for Oracle Red Labs.
#
# The shipped site has no build step and no dependencies, so the rules below
# only hide local agent-tooling artifacts: installed skills and the working
# state a design agent writes into the workspace. Everything under frontend/,
# including the css/, js/ and assets/ files that are not committed yet, is real
# source and stays visible to git.

# ---- Installed agent skills (npx skills / Agent Skills spec) ----
# .agents/skills/ holds the canonical copy of each installed skill; the
# <agent>/skills/ directories below are the symlinks (or copies) the installer
# adds for agents that keep their own skill folder. All of it is regenerated by
# `npx skills add <owner/repo>`, so per-machine installs stay out of history.
.agents/
.claude/skills/
.cursor/skills/
.codex/skills/
.gemini/skills/
.opencode/skills/
.aider-desk/skills/
.adal/skills/

# Install manifest for the skills above. Ignored so every machine keeps its own
# skill set. To version the installed skills instead, delete this rule and the
# .agents/ rule above, then commit skills-lock.json and .agents/skills/.
skills-lock.json

# ---- Design-agent working state (impeccable skill) ----
# Briefs, decision payloads, run transcripts, question logs and live-preview
# server state. The design record a run produces is delivered as DESIGN.md,
# which stays tracked. To version the raw record instead, drop these rules and
# list the state paths to hide; the skill also keeps finer-grained rules in
# .git/info/exclude.
.impeccable/
.impeccable-live.json
.impeccable-live/

# ---- Skill run dumps ----
# Concept-seed rolls the design skill drops in the repository root.
seed-roll-*.txt

# ---- Node / local application state ----
backend/node_modules/
backend/.env
backend/.env.example
backend/.env.notifications.example
backend/uploads/
backend/.tmp-mysql-data/
*.log

# ---- Generated delivery working directories ----
.codex-presentation/
.codex-finalizer/
.codex-build/
.submission-staging/

# ---- Optional: agent instruction files ----
# AGENTS.md documents this repository's conventions for coding agents. It is
# deliberately not ignored, because collaborators and their agents both need it;
# uncomment the rule below to keep it local instead.
# AGENTS.md

.env
